# The two fixes platted.toml cannot show: the abandonment overlay inside the fade ring, and an
# automatic construction clearing the vacant-Lot drawing and the foliage under it.
#
# WHY A SECOND SCRIPT. One run is one Ruleset. platted.toml is the only shipped file that states
# `[lots] storeys_per_rung`, so it is the only world with mid-rise and tower bodies -- and it
# declares no decline clock and builds its whole city at boot, so nothing in it is ever abandoned
# and nothing is ever raised. tall-declining.toml beside this file is platted.toml plus the clock.
#
# Run it from the repository root, against a RELEASE build in the directory Godot loads:
#
#   dotnet build src/Borough.Godot -c Release \
#     -p:OutputPath=$PWD/src/Borough.Godot/.godot/mono/temp/bin/Debug/
#   BOROUGH_RENDER_PROFILE=1 godot --path src/Borough.Godot -- \
#     --ruleset plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tall-declining.toml --citizens 40000 \
#     --drive plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/declining.drive \
#     > plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/declining.log 2>&1
#
# Tick 5,120 is two and a half Days in: the clock condemns after one, so the shells have been
# standing for a Day and the sweep is raising replacements. declining.log's family_body lines carry
# `abandoned`. Every shot is on a Tick that is noon -- 1,024 past a Day boundary of 2,048 -- so the
# three construction frames are lit the same way and comparing them compares the city.

1 speed 8

5100 ui family-bodies on
5100 roads on
5100 tilt 40
5100 turn right
5100 hold look

# sol-F2: Building 11, a tower-stepped-point abandoned at tile 528 560, on each side of the fade
# and in the ring. The overlay has to fade with the body it dresses rather than draw over both.
5102 focus 528 560 300
5102 click 528 560
5103 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/derelict-tower-0300.png

5104 focus 528 560 475
5104 click 528 560
5105 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/derelict-tower-0475.png
5105 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/derelict-tower-0475.json

5106 focus 528 560 1000
5106 click 528 560
5107 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/derelict-tower-1000.png

# The same in the ring for a mid-rise: Building 1, a panel-slab at tile 560 515.
5108 focus 560 515 475
5108 click 560 515
5109 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/derelict-midrise-0475.png

# sol-F3: one camera over the middle, a shot a Day. The caption's vacant Lot count moves with the
# sweep, which it cannot do unless an incremental body change refreshes the spatial passes; the
# draw lists say which Buildings are new and whether any tree stands inside one.
5110 focus 556 560 600
5120 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-0-5120.png
5121 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-0-5120.tsv

7168 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-1-7168.png
7169 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-1-7168.tsv

9216 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-2-9216.png
9217 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/build-2-9216.tsv

9218 quit
